+        <div class="settings"><div class="section-label">RENDER SETTINGS</div><label for="quality">Samples per pixel<select id="quality"><option value="16">16 · Quick</option><option value="64" selected>64 · Balanced</option><option value="256">256 · Detailed</option></select></label><div class="setting-row"><span>Resolution</span><span>640 × 480</span></div><div class="setting-row"><span>Engine</span><span class="engine"><i></i> C++ → WebAssembly</span></div></div>
+        <div class="privacy-note"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M8 21h8m-4-4v4"/></svg><span>All the magic happens on your device.<br />No servers. Just photons (sort of).</span></div>
+      </aside>
+    </section>
+    <section class="details"><div class="detail-title"><span class="tiny-label">BEHIND THE PIXELS</span><h3>Simple ingredients.<br />Beautiful complexity.</h3></div><div class="detail"><span class="detail-number">01 /</span><h4>Follow the light</h4><p>Paths of light bounce through the scene, building an image one sample at a time.</p></div><div class="detail"><span class="detail-number">02 /</span><h4>Keep it real</h4><p>Soft shadows, reflections, and refractions. Real physics, with a little randomness.</p></div><div class="detail"><span class="detail-number">03 /</span><h4>Made for your browser</h4><p>Kevin Beason’s tiny C++ renderer, compiled to WebAssembly. No installation needed.</p></div></section>
